\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 Procter & Gamble\uc2  Will Cut 7,000 Jobs\b0\par\par\uc2 By Gregory Schmidt \par \uc2 335 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 June 2025\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The reductions will come over two years as the consumer products giant seeks to reorganize.\par \par \uc2 The consumer goods giant \uc2 Procter & Gamble\uc2  said on Thursday that it would cut 7,000 jobs globally over the next two years, or 6 percent of its total work force, as it seeks to reorganize amid uncertainty caused by President Trump's trade war.\par \par \uc2 The company, which makes products like Tide laundry detergent and Pampers diapers, said at a conference in Paris that the job cuts would be combined with plans to shed brands to streamline its portfolio.\par \par \uc2 Executives did not specify which brands would be eliminated or where the job reductions would be made, but said the cuts would eliminate 15 percent of the company's nonmanufacturing work force.\par \par \uc2 ''We see more opportunities to make roles broader and teams smaller,'' \uc2 Andre Schulten\uc2 , the company's chief financial officer, said at the conference. It had about 108,000 jobs worldwide as of June 2024.\par \par \uc2 Procter & Gamble\uc2 , which is based in Cincinnati, has struggled with falling demand as consumers have remained cautious after Mr. Trump announced tariffs on America's top trading partners in April. Last month, the company lowered its sales and profit guidance for 2025.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Schulten said the uncertainty caused by tariffs, along with geopolitical tensions including conflicts in the Middle East and Ukraine, had created headwinds for the company. He added that the changes were not in response to any single factor but instead part of a longer-term ''integrated growth strategy.''\par \par \uc2 Other companies, including \uc2 General Motors\uc2  and Target, have also reduced or withdrawn their earnings guidance recently, and some have also announced layoffs. On Thursday, \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  said it would cut approximately 3,500 technology jobs in Shanghai and Dalian in China as part of a broader consolidation plan.\par \par \uc2 Procter & Gamble\uc2 's share price, which has dipped slightly over the last year, inched up 0.25 percent in premarket trading after the changes were announced.\par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020250606el660003j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
