\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 Gaming Union Reaches a Deal With \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 , Scoring a First\b0\par\par\uc2 By Karen Weise \par \uc2 481 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 May 2025\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The agreement includes across-the-board wage increases of 13.5 percent.\par \par \uc2 A union representing 300 video game workers at \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  said on Friday that it had reached a tentative agreement with the tech company on the terms of the first union contract in the gaming industry.\par \par \uc2 The Communications Workers of America, which represents the workers, announced the contract covering quality assurance employees at \uc2 ZeniMax\uc2 . The gaming publisher, which \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  bought for $7.5 billion in a deal that closed in 2021, makes blockbuster titles including The Elder Scrolls, Fallout and Doom.\par \par \uc2 The agreement includes a 13.5 percent wage increase for all workers and institutes new minimum pay for each category of jobs, the union said.\par \par \uc2 Employees in the gaming industry -- particularly those who work long hours in quality assurance, testing games for bugs and other glitches -- have been working for several years to organize over their pay and conditions.\par \par \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  makes the Xbox gaming platform and has acquired a number of gaming companies, which now make up one of its most important consumer businesses, generating $23 billion in revenue in the past four quarters.\par \par \uc2 Tech companies have typically resisted unionization. But in its 2022 acquisition of the video game maker \uc2 Activision Blizzard\uc2 , \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  agreed not to oppose union organizing as part of its campaign to gain antitrust approval for the deal. That acquisition closed for almost $70 billion in 2023, and hundreds of workers there formed a union, although they have yet to come to a contract agreement.\par \par \uc2 Employees at three \uc2 ZeniMax\uc2  locations also formed a union in 2023, called ZeniMax Workers United-CWA, in a vote that avoided a conventional union election run by the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2 . The union then began negotiating with \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The lowest-paid workers in the union at \uc2 ZeniMax\uc2  earn $20.75 an hour, said Beth Allen, a spokeswoman for the \uc2 Communications Workers of America\uc2 . That would jump to $25 an hour upon ratification of the new contract by union members, a vote expected by June 20. On July 1, an across-the-board wage increase would bring up that pay to $28.38 an hour.\par \par \uc2 ''We appreciate the dedication and engagement of the ZeniMax QA team and the bargaining committee throughout this process,'' Amy Pannoni, a vice president at \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 , said in a statement. ''The tentative agreement represents a meaningful step forward and reflects a shared commitment to constructive dialogue and a common goal of fostering a positive workplace.''\par \par \uc2 The tentative agreement also incorporates a novel provision announced in late 2023 on the use of artificial intelligence, which is expected to upend some industries by replacing or assisting workers. \uc2 ZeniMax\uc2  committed to informing the union when its plans to use A.I. could affect workers, and ''to bargain those impacts upon request,'' the union said.\par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020250531el5v0003t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
