\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECT\par \b \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  Hires \uc2 Instacart\uc2  C.E.O. to Run Business and Operations\b0\par\par\uc2 By Mike Isaac \par \uc2 562 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 May 2025\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 The New York Times on the Web\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Sam Altman\uc2 , \uc2 OpenAI\uc2 's chief executive, said he hired \uc2 Instacart\uc2 's \uc2 Fidji Simo\uc2  to join in a new role as chief executive of applications.\par \par \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  said late Wednesday that it hired \uc2 Fidji Simo\uc2 , the chief executive of \uc2 Instacart\uc2 , to take on a new role running the artificial intelligence company's business and operations teams.\par \par \uc2 In a blog post, \uc2 Sam Altman\uc2 , \uc2 OpenAI\uc2 's chief executive, said he would remain in charge as the head of the company. But Ms. Simo's appointment as chief executive of applications would free him up to focus on other parts of the organization, including research, computing and safety systems, he said.\par \par \uc2 ''We have become a global product company serving hundreds of millions of users worldwide and growing very quickly,'' Mr. Altman said in the blog post. He added that \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  had also become an ''infrastructure company'' that delivered artificial intelligence tools at scale.\par \par \uc2 ''Each of these is a massive effort that could be its own large company,'' he wrote. ''Bringing on exceptional leaders is a key part of doing that well.''\par \par \uc2 Ms. Simo, a member of \uc2 OpenAI\uc2 's board, will oversee sales, marketing and finance. She will report to Mr. Altman.\par \par \uc2 OpenAI\uc2 , which ignited a frenzy over A.I. with its ChatGPT chatbot, has grown rapidly and juggled multiple initiatives -- sometimes unsuccessfully. The San Francisco company has steadily released new A.I. models and products, including systems that can ''reason.'' In March, it completed a $40 billion fund-raising deal, led by the Japanese conglomerate SoftBank, that valued it at $300 billion and made it one of the most valuable private companies in the world.\par \par \uc2 But \uc2 OpenAI\uc2 , which was set up as a nonprofit, has struggled to adopt a new corporate structure. As the commercial appeal of artificial intelligence has grown, the company had tried to remove itself from control by the nonprofit. That attracted scrutiny from critics such as \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , an \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  founder who sued the company and accused it of putting profit ahead of A.I. safety. The attorneys general of California and Delaware also scrutinized the restructuring.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  backtracked on the plan and said it would allow the nonprofit to retain its grip on the company.\par \par \uc2 (The \uc2 New York Times\uc2  has sued \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  and its partner, \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 , accusing them of copyright infringement regarding news content related to A.I. systems. \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  and \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  have denied those claims.)\par \par \uc2 In a statement late Wednesday, Ms. Simo said that \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  ''has the potential of accelerating human potential at a pace never seen before and I am deeply committed to shaping these applications toward the public good.''\par \par \uc2 She added in a memo to \uc2 Instacart\uc2  employees that she had a ''passion for A.I. and in particular for the potential it has to cure diseases'' and that ''the ability to lead such an important part of our collective future was a hard opportunity to pass up.''\par \par \uc2 Ms. Simo will remain at \uc2 Instacart\uc2  for the next few months as the company names a successor, a role she said would be filled by a member of \uc2 Instacart\uc2 's management team. She will also remain on the company's board as its chairperson.\par \par \uc2 ''Today's announcement is not a reflection of any changes in our business or operations,'' \uc2 Instacart\uc2  said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020250508el5800051\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
