\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 UPS\uc2  Says It Will Cut 20,000 Jobs As Levies Reduce Shipping Volume\b0\par\par\uc2 By Peter Eavis \par \uc2 589 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 April 2025\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 5\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The move comes as President Trump's tariffs are reducing shipping volumes and is in addition to 12,000 job cuts last year.\par \par \uc2 UPS\uc2  said on Tuesday that it would cut 20,000 jobs this year as part of a long-term plan to reduce costs and bolster profit.\par \par \uc2 The cuts come as President Trump's tariffs are prompting some \uc2 UPS\uc2  customers to ship fewer goods. The company said ''macroeconomic uncertainty'' prevented it from updating its forecasts for revenue and profits for 2025.\par \par \uc2 UPS\uc2  already cut 12,000 jobs last year. It now has some 490,000 employees, many of whom are members of the \uc2 Teamsters union\uc2 . In its latest cuts, the company said it would shed ''operational'' employees, or those who sort or deliver packages. \uc2 UPS\uc2  also said it would close 73 buildings by the end of June.\par \par \uc2 UPS\uc2  has been trying to improve its profit margins, partly by reducing costs and shedding parts of its business that don't make money. The company has said many of the deliveries it does for \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , its largest customer, are not profitable. It plans to slash in half the volume of packages it delivers for \uc2 Amazon\uc2  by the middle of next year.\par \par \uc2 In all, \uc2 UPS\uc2  plans to reduce costs by $3.5 billion this year. Most of that sum is expected to come from the job cuts and building closures, but the company also anticipates savings from reducing the number of hours its employees work. \uc2 UPS\uc2  has 412,000 hourly employees, about half of whom are part time.\par \par \uc2 In 2023, the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  and \uc2 UPS\uc2  agreed to a five-year labor contract that included wages that were significantly higher than at nonunion delivery companies. Commenting on the job cuts Tuesday, the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 ' general president, Sean M. O'Brien, said the contract requires \uc2 UPS\uc2  to create 30,000 Teamster jobs.\par \par \uc2 ''If \uc2 UPS\uc2  wants to continue to downsize corporate management, the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  won't stand in its way,'' Mr. O'Brien said in a news release. ''But if the company intends to violate our contract or makes any attempt to go after hard-fought, good-paying \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  jobs, \uc2 UPS\uc2  will be in for a hell of a fight.''\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 UPS\uc2  spokesman said the company would adhere to the contract.\par \par \uc2 On a call with investors Tuesday, \uc2 UPS\uc2 's chief executive, \uc2 Carol Tom\u233\'00\'E9\uc2 , said Mr. Trump's trade policies were particularly debilitating for small and midsize businesses that buy goods from China. The president has raised tariffs by as much as 145 percent on many goods imported from that country.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Tom\u233\'00\'E9 said smaller companies, which didn't have the financial wherewithal to stock up before the tariffs took effect, are now saying, ''Wow, how are we going to handle this cost increase that's coming our way?''\par \par \uc2 Ms. Tom\u233\'00\'E9 said deliveries from China to the United States were \uc2 UPS\uc2 's most profitable trade lane and responsible for 11 percent of the company's international revenue. The company said it expected its China-to-United States business to decline.\par \par \uc2 But Ms. Tom\u233\'00\'E9 also said \uc2 UPS\uc2  would be able to respond to any shift in supply chains caused by the tariffs. In Mr. Trump's first term, Chinese exports to the United States declined, but trade grew between China and rest of the world, she said, noting that \uc2 UPS\uc2 's international business also grew in that period.\par \par \uc2 ''We can move where supply chains move,'' Ms. Tom\u233\'00\'E9 said.\par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020250430el4u0004d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
