\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 The Digest\b0\par\par\uc2 By Reuters and The Associated Press \par \uc2 473 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 March 2025\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MARKETS\par \par \uc2 Nasdaq Chooses Texas\par \par \uc2 For Regional Headquarters\par \par \uc2 Nasdaq said on Tuesday that it would open a regional headquarters in Texas, deepening its presence in a state that is fast emerging as a major financial hub rivaling New York.\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 -led \uc2 Tesla\uc2  and \uc2 SpaceX\uc2 , as well as the tech giants \uc2 Oracle\uc2  and \uc2 Hewlett Packard Enterprise\uc2 , have all moved to the Lone Star State in recent years, attracted by a favorable tax climate, lower costs of living and reduced energy costs.\par \par \uc2 The move could also help Nasdaq better compete with the New York Stock Exchange -- which last month committed to launching an exchange in the state -- and the Texas Stock Exchange, a venture backed by \uc2 BlackRock\uc2  and \uc2 Citadel Securities\uc2 , which is gearing up for a launch next year.\par \par \uc2 '' We're proud to be leading the way in cementing Dallas as the financial capital of the world,'' a spokesperson for the Texas Stock Exchange's parent company, TXSE, said. REUTERS\par \par \uc2 INTERNATIONAL\par \par \uc2 Siemens\uc2  to Cut 8% of Jobs\par \par \uc2 At Its Digital Industries\par \par \uc2 Siemens\uc2  will cut 5,600 jobs at its Digital Industries business, the engineering company said on Tuesday, in the latest blow for German industry shaken by weak demand at home and abroad.\par \par \uc2 The job cuts amount to a little more than 8 percent of the 68,000 people employed in Digital Industries globally, and come as \uc2 Siemens\uc2  adjusts its production capacity in line with weak market conditions in Germany and China.\par \par \uc2 It is the biggest number of layoffs announced by \uc2 Siemens\uc2  since 2017, with 2,600 of the jobs being axed in Germany, although \uc2 Siemens\uc2  said it was still committed to its home country as a business location.\par \par \uc2 Until recently Digital Industries had been the jewel in \uc2 Siemens\uc2 's crown, with the highest margins in the group for its controllers and factory software.\par \par \uc2 REUTERS\par \par \uc2 ENTERTAINMENT\par \par \uc2 Movie Theater Alliance Has a New Name for Itself\par \par \uc2 In hindsight, \uc2 NATO\uc2  was an unnecessarily confusing acronym for a trade organization representing movie theater owners. For 60 years, the \uc2 National Association of Theatre Owners\uc2  has promoted interests of movie theaters. They've also been confused with the other \uc2 NATO\uc2 , the \uc2 North Atlantic Treaty Organization\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But the theater owner's organization is looking to the future, with a new name and a refocused mission. The group will now be known as Cinema United, president and C.E.O. \uc2 Michael O'Leary\uc2  said Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 ''It can be a little complicated having the same name as a multinational military alliance,'' Mr. O'Leary said. ''We felt that it was time to look at our name and do a rebrand.''\par \par \uc2 Cinema United represents over 32,000 movie screens in the U.S. and over 30,000 more in 88 other countries. Moviegoing, the new tagline reads, is their mission.\par \par \uc2 ASSOCIATED PRESS\par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020250319el3j0004w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
